    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "Spanish participles ending in *-ado* or *-ido* can function as adjectives when used with the verbs *ser* or *estar*. \nWhen functioning as adjectives, they agree in gender and number with the noun they modify, as in *Las camas están arregladas* ('The beds are made'). \nWhen used with *haber* in perfect tenses, participles remain invariable."
    }
